---
/**
 * THE OUTSIDE LINK ON AN OPENING FRAME — applied from preview/ab-zw13,
 * THE INLINE, on 2026-10-06, chosen from fourteen built as real pages.
 *
 * It replaces `.still__go`, which was a translucent pill: a 1px 50%-white
 * border, a 35% ground and a 6px backdrop-filter holding a 10px mono label.
 *
 * WHY THE PILL WENT, AND IT IS A MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN A PREFERENCE. That
 * chrome exists to hold white type off a bright photograph, and the corner it
 * sat in is the DARKEST part of the frame it sat on. Read off Aasha's opening
 * still — 2880x2160, exactly its declared 4:3, so `cover` crops nothing — the
 * button's own box measures mean .0077 and p95 .0168 relative luminance,
 * where white reads 18.2:1 and 15.7:1 against a 4.5:1 floor. There was
 * nothing for the plate to do. Every draft in that round started there.
 *
 * TWO TIERS OUT OF UGAM'S OWN LABEL, RE-SET AND NEVER REWRITTEN. The markdown
 * says `label: "Watch on ZEE5"` and `platform: "ZEE5"`; this splits the one on
 * the other, so the lead sets small and the destination sets large. It splits
 * ONLY when the label actually ends with the platform name — otherwise the
 * whole label goes on one line and the lead is omitted. Nothing is invented
 * and nothing is dropped, which is the same contract `cut()` and `clauses()`
 * keep on the About movements.
 *
 * <- THE VERB IS NOT "WATCH". Four of the six that render this say "Watch on",
 *   two say "Listen on", and Diwali — which files its link in the Watch
 *   section rather than here — says "View on". The draft hardcoded "Watch on"
 *   because it only ever ran on Aasha. Deriving it is what makes this safe on
 *   the whole route, and a seventh work with a different verb needs no edit.
 *
 * THE TRIANGLE IS SIZED IN em AND THAT IS THE POINT OF ZW13. 0.56em wide by
 * 0.68em tall against the platform word, so it tracks the type at every width
 * with no second breakpoint to keep in step. Measured: a 51.2px word gives
 * 28.7x34.8 and a 32px word gives 17.9x21.8 — 0.56 and 0.68 of the word in
 * both cases. The other thirteen drafts size their marks in pixels and have
 * to restate them on mobile; this one cannot drift.
 *
 * ITS BASELINE IS SET WITH vertical-align AND A SMALL translate, not with a
 * margin: the glyph has to sit on the letters' own baseline, and a margin
 * would move the line box instead of the mark inside it.
 *
 * <- THE ARROW STAYS, AND ON A BARE STILL IT IS LOAD-BEARING. Nothing on these
 *   pages plays: four of the six are bare stills whose opening is `still`, and
 *   pressing this opens the platform in a new tab. A play triangle promises
 *   inline playback, so the arrow is the only mark in the lockup saying the
 *   press goes elsewhere. Do not drop it without replacing what it says.
 *
 * <- AND IT NO LONGER MATCHES `.facade__play`. HANDOFF §5 recorded that the
 *   still's button deliberately copied the facade's — same inset, border,
 *   ground and blur — so that a still which links out and a video which plays
 *   read as one control doing two jobs. That pairing is broken by this change
 *   and the break is deliberate but UNRESOLVED: eight work pages still carry
 *   the pill on their video facade. Either the facade follows this, or the two
 *   controls are meant to differ now because only one of them plays. Flagged
 *   for Ugam; nothing in VideoFacade.astro was touched.
 */
interface Props {
  /** The work's own `external.label`, as written. */
  label: string;
  /** The work's own `external.platform`, as written. */
  platform: string;
  url: string;
}
const { label, platform, url } = Astro.props;

/* Split only on a real match; never manufacture a lead. */
const splits = label.endsWith(platform) && label.length > platform.length;
const lead = splits ? label.slice(0, -platform.length).trim() : '';
const tail = splits ? platform : label;
---

<a class="wm" href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
  {lead && <span class="wm__k">{lead}</span>}
  <span class="wm__p"><i class="wm__tri" aria-hidden="true"></i>{tail}<i
      class="wm__a" aria-hidden="true">&nearr;</i></span>
</a>

<style>
  /* The frame is `position: relative`; this sits in its bottom-left corner at
     the same inset the pill used, so nothing else on the page moves. */
  .wm {
    position: absolute;
    left: var(--margin);
    bottom: var(--margin);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 10px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--bone);
  }
  .wm__k {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--t-micro);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bone-dim);
    transition: color var(--d-micro) var(--ease);
  }
  .wm:hover .wm__k { color: var(--bone); }

  /* --wm-size lets a caller step the type down for a smaller frame. The
     default is the size the draft was judged at. */
  .wm__p {
    position: relative;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: var(--wm-size, clamp(2rem, 4.4vw, 3.2rem));
    line-height: 0.92;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* SIZED IN em SO IT TRACKS THE WORD — see the header. vertical-align sits it
     on the letters' baseline; a margin would move the line box instead. */
  .wm__tri {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.56em;
    height: 0.68em;
    background: currentColor;
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, 100% 50%, 0 100%);
    vertical-align: baseline;
    transform: translateY(0.02em);
    margin-right: 0.22em;
    transition: transform var(--d-micro) var(--ease);
  }
  .wm:hover .wm__tri { transform: translate(0.06em, 0.02em); }

  /* Drawn rather than text-decoration, so it can arrive from nothing and sit
     where this design wants it rather than at the font's underline offset. */
  .wm__p::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    bottom: -0.1em;
    height: 2px;
    background: currentColor;
    transform: scaleX(0);
    transform-origin: left;
    transition: transform var(--d-micro) var(--ease);
  }
  .wm:hover .wm__p::after { transform: scaleX(1); }

  .wm__a {
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.34em;
    vertical-align: 0.9em;
    margin-left: 0.34em;
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform var(--d-micro) var(--ease);
  }
  .wm:hover .wm__a { transform: translate(3px, -3px); }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .wm__tri,
    .wm__p::after,
    .wm__a { transition: none; }
    .wm:hover .wm__tri { transform: translateY(0.02em); }
  }

  /* The inset the pill used below 901px, kept so this change moves nothing
     but the control's own treatment. The mark needs no entry here: it is
     em-sized and follows the word down on its own. */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .wm { left: var(--s-3); bottom: var(--s-3); gap: 7px; }
  }
</style>
